# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Catering delivery vars are SERVER-ONLY (no NEXT_PUBLIC_), so
# no email address or API key ships in the client bundle.

# --- Catering inquiry delivery, via Resend (https://resend.com) -----------
# Setup (one-time, K13-owned "K13 Studio" Resend team, Transactional Pro plan).
# Note Pro is $20/mo on the TRANSACTIONAL tab; the $40 tier is Marketing, a different product.
#
#   1. Verify the subdomain notify.lobsterlab.us in Resend, NOT the root domain.
#      House convention across every K13 project. Two reasons:
#        - The root runs the client's Google Workspace. Sending as catering@lobsterlab.us
#          would collide the day they create a real mailbox at that address.
#        - Resend's records (MX + SPF on `send`, DKIM on resend._domainkey) then sit under
#          the subdomain and never touch the root SPF, which here is
#          v=spf1 include:_spf.google.com ~all and carries their live email.
#   2. Create an API key with permission `sending_access` scoped to that domain_id, so a key
#      leaked from this deployment cannot send as another K13 client.
#   3. Fill in the three values below and redeploy. Env changes alone do not rebuild.
#
# Until these are set the route FAILS the submission with 503 not_configured, rather than
# telling the visitor "sent" while the enquiry is dropped.

RESEND_API_KEY=
# Where catering inquiries are delivered. A client-owned inbox, never a K13 one.
CATERING_TO_EMAIL=info@lobsterlab.us
# Sender. House convention is <form-type>@notify.<domain>, with the brand and the form type
# in the display name. The form type is in the ADDRESS, not just the display name, so the
# client can filter catering to their events manager without asking us to change anything.
# Never noreply@: it hurts deliverability, and it is untrue here since Reply-To is set to
# the person who submitted the form.
CATERING_FROM_EMAIL="Lobster Lab Catering <catering@notify.lobsterlab.us>"

# --- Ordering storefronts are NOT env vars ---------------------------------
# They live per-location in lib/content.ts under `locations[].ordering`, because
# each of the 5 locations has its own Toast / DoorDash / Grubhub storefront and
# they are public URLs, not secrets. To connect one, paste its URL there.
# An empty string renders an honest "coming soon" state, never a dead link.
# See tasks/todo.md, phase P1.
